            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0439" n="323" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.7111/58.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Page to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 252.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my telegrams of February
                    21 and February 23, and to my despatch No. 251 of the 21st instant, I have the
                    honor to transmit herewith enclosed a copy of a note I have just received from
                    the Foreign Office to the effect that enquiries have been made of the Governor
                    of the Gold Coast Colony as to the authenticity of the leases which the negro
                    Sam purports to have acquired in the Colony, which have resulted in the
                    Governor’s answer by telegraph that the leases in question have not been
                    registered in the Gold Coast.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walter Hines Page</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d473-a1.xml" xpointer="d473-a1"/>
            </div>
